          "filename": "The Sweet House of the Past.jpg",
          "caption": "Victor Gaston Ancestral House, or popularly known as Balay Negrenese, is the most visited ancestral house in Silay City, Negros Occidental. It is also one of the most popular ancestral houses in the province. It was initially built in 1897, but it was only completed in 1901. It is a symbol of Negros Occidental's rich past, where sugar production was in demand at that time. It is also a symbol of the Negrenses' preservation of the past that this house is a living witness  rich history and culture of the Negrenses.",
